      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Aceclofenac, a phenylacetic acid derivative, is a new nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID). It is indicated in the symptomatic treatment of pain and inflammatory or degenerative arthropathies: osteoarthritis, rheumatoid arthritis, ankylosing spondylitis, abarticular inflammations, posttrauma or postoperative inflammations. The usual oral dosage of aceclofenac is 100 mg twice daily in adults. Its clinical efficacy seems to be similar to that of other NSAIDs, but its safety profile, especially gastro-intestinal tolerance, appears to be better. Finally, in vitro studies suggested that aceclofenac may exert positive effect on cartilage matrix metabolism."},
